    {
      "id": "increment.v11-o5-phase-semantics",
      "state": "active",
      "correctionClass": "o5-premeasurement-terminal-and-cross-os-verification-phase-separation",
      "observedProblem": "O5 currently names an exact release candidate commit and tag as a pre-registration field even though the candidate must include later task evidence, making exact premeasurement binding causally impossible or inviting a vague placeholder. It also says every claimed operating-system family reproduces verification from a clean checkout while live G3 re-verification intentionally depends on a Windows protected source, so the text can be read as requiring impossible private-source replication or overclaiming full accepted verification on other systems.",
      "hypothesis": "Renaming the pre-registration field to an exact candidate-and-tag derivation rule and separating evidence-holder terminal re-verification from per-OS public contract plus task-scoped mechanism reproduction will preserve the same O5 threshold while making both phases machine-expressible and claims accurately bounded.",
      "falsifier": "Stop or revise if the repair permits post-result tag or candidate cherry-picking, weakens clean-checkout or cross-OS behavior evidence, copies private cohort evidence to another operating system, implies non-Windows live G3 verification, changes cohort sample thresholds or human authority, creates a task validator before a natural O5 task, performs a release, or produces any O1-O5 progress.",
      "stopCondition": "Stop after O5 pre-registration binds an immutable candidate/tag derivation and no-mutation rule rather than an unknowable exact commit; terminal exact commit/tag remain bound only in the candidate and human release gate; each claimed OS must reproduce public non-private contract checks and task-scoped activation/rollback/cleanup while the authorized evidence-holder surface alone performs live private-source terminal re-verification; cross-OS behavior remains task-validator evidence; criteria digest, verifier, docs and full tests align at O1-O5 0/5; residue is absent; and this increment exits the graph.",
      "acceptanceIds": [
        "G1",
        "G2",
        "G3",
        "G4"
      ],
      "taskRegistration": null,
